  "source_review": [
    "SecurityConfiguration still checks token-derived X-CSRF-Token for ambient browser-cookie mutations before dispatch; Bearer and internal service-key requests have explicit credentials.",
    "All 11 GET traces still conflate UpstreamGuard.Operation receivers with a distinct AgentClient streaming operation. execute calls the supplied Operation instance. Capability dispatch cannot supply assistant/task BiConsumer callbacks. Public map quotas, cache writes, metrics and lazy RAG initialization remain real bounded side effects, not assistant conversation mutations.",
    "Changed photoImage trace now goes through AmapGateway.imageFromPoi at lines 357/366. Its supplied operation only reserves map quota, sends image HTTP GET and reads a bounded body within try-with-resources. No assistant/task mutation callback is supplied. The other branch still uses the ordinary AgentClient.post operation. Four fresh trace paths and their original severities are retained.",
    "Five reported version response/audit expressions remain dominated by successful atomic SQL INTEGER version=version+1 and rowcount checks inside the corresponding transaction. INT exhaustion would fail the SQL update; this is not a claim of unlimited version lifetime.",
    "Totp.encrypt production caller remains AccountSecurityService.enroll with server-generated 20-byte base32 seed (32 ASCII characters), 12-byte nonce and 16-byte GCM tag. No HTTP-controlled plaintext length reaches the allocation.",
    "Two Math.random results remain test-username uniqueness in the Playwright operations fixture. Server-issued bearer tokens and production credentials do not use that PRNG.",
    "optimization_seed_admin prints only the returned status/boolean aggregate; synthetic passwords and TOTP seed are written to its guarded ignored fixture file, not returned metadata.",
    "Installer chmod 0755 still applies only to a fresh root-owned public Debian package download directory in an explicitly opted-in image build. The active Dockerfile now adds separate stable native backports; neither changes this chmod target into credential storage."
  ],
